codex
The shared post-auth failure is another native distlib detail: `csk.exe`’s embedded `__main__.py` deliberately rewrites `sys.argv[0]` to sibling `csk` (without `.exe`). The worker then tried to identity-check a nonexistent path. I’m adding a strict Windows-only `.exe` normalization from the actual argv0—no PATH lookup or environment input—and extending the worker interpreter check to the already-bound base executable.
