The first macOS attempt failed before worker launch because I created the validation venv with `--copies`; on macOS that turns the copied launcher itself into the apparent Python home, where no standard library exists. This is a test-environment construction error, not a product failure. I’m preserving that red JUnit and recreating the fresh venv with the platform’s normal canonical framework symlink, which is the same supported layout used by the prior native review.
