codex
The macOS product failure was resource exhaustion in the retained identity monitor: the guard correctly watches every bound stdlib/package/tool path, but the host’s default soft descriptor limit is 256 while the bound set is about 2,600 paths. I’ve added a bounded, operation-serialized macOS guard that raises only the manager’s soft descriptor capacity for the monitor lifetime and restores the exact prior limit at teardown. The transient mutate-and-restore semantics remain intact; focused tests now include the raise/restore invariant and pass.
