 - LAUNCHER IDENTITY: distlib removes `.exe` from `sys.argv[0]` before `csk.cli.main`; fixed Windows-only suffix restoration recovers the bound launcher without consulting `PATH`, environment, package input, or user options.
 - IMPORT TCB: base CPython necessarily places `python_home` on `sys.path`. Admitting it without binding it would allow root-level code before worker proof, so the complete bounded Windows Python-home import tree is now identity-bound while disabled site-package directories remain excluded. Tester regressions first failed 2/2 (exit 1) on stale manager/worker root validation and omitted fixed `python314.zip`, then passed 2/2 (exit 0) after exact-root deserialization and fixed-slot archive binding.
 - NATIVE HOSTS: exact candidate 8 exited 0 on macOS with 10 passed / no skips in 63.985 seconds and on Windows with 5 passed / 5 host-specific skips in 287.548 seconds; all three Windows accepted variants built and the hidden-literal/runtime-image negatives passed. A separate tester-owned Windows plain accepted gate on the same candidate exited 0 with 1 passed / no skips in 62.09 seconds. Output was validated and never executed.
-- LOCAL GATES: focused driver pytest exited 0 with 119 passed / 1 platform skip; strict mypy exited 0 over 65 source files; compileall, tabnanny, tracked diff hygiene, and explicit new-file whitespace/conflict scanning exited 0. Exact whole-module unit branch coverage measured 54% (3,093 statements, 1,313 missed; 1,050 branches, 214 partial), so no 80% whole-file coverage claim is made.
